 # json-toolkit
 
+Documentation version: 0.2.0 (2026-10-28)
+
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
@@ -19,3 +21,11 @@ updated copy of the JSON document. The original document is never mutated. The p
 `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, and `test`; malformed patches and unsuccessful operations throw
 an error. Both inputs must contain only JSON values (null, booleans, finite numbers, strings, arrays,
 and objects); non-JSON JavaScript values and cyclic structures are rejected.
+
+### `applyMergePatch(target, patch)`
+
+Applies an [RFC 7386 JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386) document and returns
+an updated copy of the target. An object patch merges recursively; its members whose values are
+`null` remove the corresponding target members. A non-object patch replaces the target entirely.
+Both inputs must contain only JSON values (null, booleans, finite numbers, strings, arrays, and
+objects); non-JSON JavaScript values and cyclic structures are rejected. Neither input is mutated.
